  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "No automatic AWS delivery on push",
      "items": [
        "Validate runs on PR/push; Manual Build also invokes that gate before publisher OIDC credentials.",
        "Build publishes the commit-pinned image once and records its digest. The published digest is scanned; a failed scan blocks Release. Create Release rechecks successful Build evidence, ECR scans and the environment contract.",
        "The release is a data-only S3 bundle identified by key, VersionId and SHA256. It is not code fetched ad hoc by management."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "A narrow trust handoff",
      "items": [
        "Publisher and orchestrator are separate OIDC roles. The orchestrator can invoke the fixed document on the approved management host.",
        "A new DeploymentId and actual ExpectedPreviousRevision prevent ambiguous/replayed operations. Management reads the exact artifact version.",
        "GitHub has no direct network path to the Kubernetes API. Management executes pinned Helm and records the operation receipt."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Strict convergence and smoke",
      "items": [
        "LBC injects target-health readiness gates on new pods in the labelled namespace. Healthy ALB targets allow pod readiness and replacement of old pods.",
        "Smoke requires KUBERNETES_READY, AUTH_BACKEND_REACHABLE and EDGE_ANONYMOUS_REJECTED. Auth refresh must return HTTP 400 with valid ProblemDetails and X-Request-Id.",
        "5xx never passes. A mutated failure invokes bounded Helm rollback and verification; PostgreSQL migrations are not reverted."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "PROVEN · 29 October 2026",
      "items": [
        "First delivery: revisions 1 → 2 → 3; Auth smoke received ALB 504 and automatic rollback was VERIFIED.",
        "After readiness-gate injection was demonstrated: v2.0.8 delivery 3 → 4 succeeded with six Ready pods and new healthy target IPs.",
        "The executor diagnostic patch remains local and is not presented as installed runtime behavior."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Evidence and current state",
      "items": [
        "DECLARED: arrows describe source-backed design; the reading guide gives the source for each relationship.",
        "OBSERVED: topology captured on 28–29 October 2026. Runtime retired on 29 October; RDS retained stopped.",
        "PROVEN applies only to named experiments. These diagrams are not live telemetry or a production certification."
      ]
    }
